(:id "port/python/packet/ranged-integers" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/kind_int.go" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_ranged_bits_test.go: TestPythonPacketRangedBits, TestPythonPacketRangedBitsNegativeControl" "make/python.mk: python-packet-ranged-bits-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "9b6e1bf5e466b9a9bf59d366eac5716b17d96f90" :note "2026-11-15: every carried golden that declares a ranged integer reads and writes back byte-identical under both pins, each declared minimum and maximum round-trips, every below-minimum, above-maximum and non-int write raises InvalidValue, and a non-canonical offset, a truncated input and a trailing byte refuse. The negative control rewrites a copy of the generated ProbeBits reader and the gate goes red on its write-back marker. Run on macOS arm64 with the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, and make generated-current, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/packet/bits" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/kind_bits.go" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_ranged_bits_test.go: TestPythonPacketRangedBits, TestPythonPacketRangedBitsNegativeControl" "make/python.mk: python-packet-ranged-bits-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "9b6e1bf5e466b9a9bf59d366eac5716b17d96f90" :note "2026-11-15: the bits(N) emitter reads every width class from 1 to 64 bits, ProbeBits and BenchBits come off the golden harness's skip list and round-trip byte-identical under both pins, declared boundaries round-trip, out-of-range and non-int writes raise InvalidValue, and truncated input, trailing bytes and nonzero padding refuse. The negative control rewrites a copy of the generated ProbeBits reader and the gate goes red on its write-back marker. Run on macOS arm64 with the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, and make generated-current, at this revision.")
